{
  "dom_id": "step-76960",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Evaluating Expressions With Multiple Variables",
  "problem": "Evaluate $\\dfrac{n-2}{m-1} + \\dfrac{2(m+1)}{n}$ for $m=4$ and $n=6.$",
  "worked_solution": "We replace $m$ with $4$ and $n$ with $6$ in the expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{n-2}{m-1}+\\frac{2(m+1)}{n} & = \\\\ \\frac{6-2}{4-1}+\\frac{2(4+1)}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{2(5)}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{10}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{5}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{4+5}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{9}{3} & = \\\\ 3 & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
